dArkOS: ScreenScraper's developer login is no longer only what the build was given.
- The user's own comes first (es_settings.cfg: ScreenScraperDevId and
  ScreenScraperDevPassword).
- Then the build's (exports.sh, DEV_ID/DEV_PASS), if ScreenScraper takes it: it is
  asked once (ssinfraInfos), as a login in an image can go out of date. With no
  answer at all it is kept.
- Otherwise the scraper fetches the one RetroGameSets' RGSX hands out
  (retrogamesets.fr, a friendly project), once per run while its server answers.
A check or fetch with no answer (curl, 5 s) is tried again a minute later, and the
login is kept in memory only. An image built without exports.sh had no login at
all, and every scrape failed with "Erreur de login : Vérifier vos identifiants
développeur".

